<h1>recursion tree</h1>
<p>
(definition)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Definition:</strong>
A method to analyze the <a href="complexity.html"><em>complexity</em></a> of an <a href="algorithm.html"><em>algorithm</em></a> by diagramming the <a href="recursive.html"><em>recursive</em></a> function calls.
</p>

<p>
<strong>Formal Definition:</strong> A recursion tree T(p) of degree p is either (i) <a href="nulltree.html"><em>null</em></a> or (ii) has p <a href="child.html"><em>children</em></a> which are recursion trees.
</p>

<p>
<em>Note:
Also known as an "R-tree".</em>
</p>

<p>Author: <a href="../Other/contrib.html#authorPEB">PEB</a></p>
<h2>More information</h2>
<p>
After <a href="../terms.html#GCG92">[GCG92]</a> and <a href="../terms.html#CLR90">[CLR90, page 59]</a>.  Suggested by Rama Maiti, 19 August 2001.
</p>

